.TH GXWI-HELLO 1 2026-10-19 "Peios gxwi 0.0.7"
.SH NAME
gxwi-hello \- display a diagnostic GXWI session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gxwi-hello
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gxwi-hello
is a diagnostic compositor started by gxwid when no compositor path is configured.
It receives a session listener from peinit and displays the identity and token properties of its process.
It also provides a WebSocket echo endpoint and an action that ends the session.
.PP
This program verifies the session transport and identity path.
It is not a desktop shell or application launcher.
.SH SECURITY
The inherited session listener is protected for the daemon's use.
The program restamps the listener with its own identity before serving.
Displayed identity comes from the process token rather than browser-provided input.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The diagnostic sign-out action ended the process or the service loop completed.
.TP
.B 1
No listener was supplied, or listener setup or serving failed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LISTEN_FDS
Must name at least one inherited descriptor.
The first listener is descriptor 3.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gxwid (8),
.BR gxwi-hello-app (1)
